Displaced Avenger wrote:
> Tars Tarkas wrote:
>> Hi!
>>
>> The updated, new and improved Seppuku Patch is now available for
>> Nethack 3.4.3.
>>
>> Description:
>> This patch allows a Samurai to commit Seppuku (ritual suicide, a.k.a
>> hara kiri) by (a)pplying a sword.
>> This requires you to have a sword (obviously) and to be able to wield
>> it as your primary weapon. If you're not wearing an Amulet of Lifesaving,
>> you die from this, are made lawful if you weren't, the anger of
>> Amaterasu Omikami is set to none and your alignment is set to maximum.
>> You also do not lose the 10% score you would if you were killed by some
>> other means. Roleplaying your Samurai will thus be rewarded.
>> If you were wearing an Amulet of Lifesaving, then your life is saved as
>> usual and:
>>     * Lawful Samurai: Alignemnt decrease by 10, Luck decrease by 5
>>     * Neutral Samurai: No change
>>     * Chaotic Samurai: Alignment increase by 10, Luck increase by 5
> 
> I'm not sure I understand the intent of this patch.  Is it just to add
> another unique death to Nethack, or is this action supposed to be
> useful in some specific situation?  The only one I can think of is if
> you know you don't have max luck, you've got an amulet of lifesaving
> on, and you're about to die (food poisoning, sliming, etc.)--and you're
> chaotic, which requires either a permanent conversion or a HoOA.
> Pretty darn rare, wouldn't you say?
> 
> -Displaced Avenger
> 
Which is exactly the point. Nethack is about gameplay, the complexity of 
the game, and building a game which can provide seemingly unique 
experiences. In the tournament, counting the player with the largest 
number of unique deaths is possible due to the depth of the game. (the 
tournament did not create a need for unique deaths; the game created the 
possiblity of counting unique deaths) This patch adds depth and 
uniqueness -- specifically adding an element which is perfectly 
applicable to only this character class.


